WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.840
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:00.840 --> 00:00:02.430
SPEAKER: We want to
make AI technology

00:00:02.430 --> 00:00:05.370
for image analysis easily
accessible for enterprises.

00:00:05.370 --> 00:00:08.430
So we created Cloud
AutoML Vision.

00:00:08.430 --> 00:00:11.340
Currently, to perform image
analysis on Google Cloud

00:00:11.340 --> 00:00:13.920
Platform, developers
can use the Vision API

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:16.712
to access a pre-trained
model or design and train

00:00:16.712 --> 00:00:20.040
a custom model with Cloud
Machine Learning Engine.

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:21.780
Let's say you're a
meteorologist and want

00:00:21.780 --> 00:00:24.420
to train a model to identify
different types of clouds--

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:27.150
like cumulus,
cumulonimbus, or stratus--

00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:30.920
to predict upcoming weather
patterns or flight plans.

00:00:30.920 --> 00:00:32.840
If you tried this
with the Vision API,

00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:34.710
here are the labels
you'd get back.

00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:36.540
It wasn't trained
specifically to identify

00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:38.255
different types of clouds.

00:00:38.255 --> 00:00:39.630
What if you want
to train a model

00:00:39.630 --> 00:00:41.910
to classify images
specific to your dataset,

00:00:41.910 --> 00:00:44.350
without writing model code?

00:00:44.350 --> 00:00:47.040
Cloud AutoML Vision lets
businesses and developers

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:50.010
with limited machine learning
expertise train custom vision

00:00:50.010 --> 00:00:51.960
models for their own use cases.

00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:55.311
Developers can upload their own
labeled or unlabeled data set,

00:00:55.311 --> 00:00:57.810
train and manage their models,
and use those models directly

00:00:57.810 --> 00:01:00.118
from the Cloud to
make predictions.

00:01:00.118 --> 00:01:01.420
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:01:01.420 --> 00:01:03.990
Let's take a look
at the AutoML UI.

00:01:03.990 --> 00:01:07.830
Begin by uploading your
images to Cloud AutoML.

00:01:07.830 --> 00:01:11.220
Then, press the Train button
to train a custom model

00:01:11.220 --> 00:01:13.230
on your image data set.

00:01:13.230 --> 00:01:15.570
When training completes,
analysis and stats

00:01:15.570 --> 00:01:17.910
of the model quality
are available directly

00:01:17.910 --> 00:01:20.610
in the AutoML UI.

00:01:20.610 --> 00:01:24.080
Next, use your model to generate
a prediction on new data,

00:01:24.080 --> 00:01:26.940
either in the UI or with
a simple REST API call.

00:01:29.470 --> 00:01:31.680
This process is easy
from start to finish.

00:01:31.680 --> 00:01:34.800
Simply upload your data
and Cloud AutoML Vision

00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:36.660
will handle scalably
training and serving

00:01:36.660 --> 00:01:39.540
the high quality model.

00:01:39.540 --> 00:01:41.503
You can learn more here.

